    "result_text": "The only concrete test class is `AcceptanceTest` (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper), and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit requirement in `OwnerRestControllerV1` \u2014 the controller backing `POST /api/owners`:\n\n1. **Added a dedicated `AUDIT` logger** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:29-30`):\n   ```java\n   private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");\n   ```\n\n2. **Emit the audit line right after a successful save** (`addOwner`), carrying the owner id, customer code, and registration date:\n   ```java\n   this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);\n   AUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n       owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n\nThe line is emitted only on the successful-create path (after all validation/quota checks and the save), so no audit line is written for rejected requests. The observed log confirms the format:\n\n```\nINFO  AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-10\n```\n\nThe test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`).",
